  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post-merge gate on `8719d8b7a` failed in two UI tests of `crates/ui/src/detect_holes_note_tests.rs`.\n\nCause: PR #1839 (#1566, merge `56ee418b`) changed the Bore law on purpose. In `crates/motion/src/machining2d/bore_core.rs`, `bore_leaves_core` now reads `bore_ring_count(...).is_none()`. Bore clears a wide hole with concentric rings. A hole is refused only past 4096 rings, or when the tool has no floor band. In `crates/app/src/operation/bore_reach.rs`, `keep_borable` uses the same plan. A 4 mm end mill now keeps the Ø74.3 hole. The two UI tests still expected the old one-ring limit (Ø12).\n\nWhich side was wrong: the tests. The product refuses each hole that the ring plan cannot clear, so no refusal was lost.\n\nThe tests now pin the new law:\n- The fixture tool is a Ø10 bull-nose with a 4.999 mm corner (`BB-1000-R1` with its corner changed).\n- A Ø74.3 through hole is stored. The corner reaches R3.001 at the floor plane, so the plan uses 14 rings.\n- A Ø24 blind hole is skipped by name. Its floor band is R0.001, so it needs 8750 rings. The limit is Ø16.554.\n- A plate with only the blind hole is refused, and nothing is stored.\n\nThe fixture builder now takes a blind floor height for each cell. The `#[test]` count stays at two.\n\nDecision entry: `docs/decisions/1909-bore-wide-hole-tests.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Both tests pass locally. Each test takes about 0.02 s.\n- The 78 s in the post-merge log is not the cost of the tests. Locally, the old failing tests also ended in 0.01 s. No heavy-lane move is necessary.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_wide_through_hole_and_names_the_one_past_the_ring_budget`\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_hole_past_the_ring_budget_is_refused`\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate test detect_holes_on_a_bore_op --crate camcraft-ui` is green on the final head. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full ui suites and the batch tier. The next post-merge run checks them.\n- The zero-floor-band refusal (a ball nose at a blind floor). The Bore tool door refuses a ball nose at create, so the UI cannot reach it. The app unit test `detect_refuses_a_blind_ball_floor_but_keeps_the_through_hole` pins it.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- #1910: the `detect_holes` row of the camcraft-mcp skill still states the one-ring limit. That file is a process file, so it is not in this PR.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1909\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
